  [ Halhadus ]
  * Created changelog
  * Vibra fixed for marble

  [ Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) ]
  * [libdroid] Initial release.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [ci] Add circelci configs.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [leds] Add DroidLedsKind and droid_leds_is_kind_supported()
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [libdroid] Release 0.0.2.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [tools] backlight: add new option --info.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [leds] set_backlight: use FLASH_TYPE_NONE.
    FLASH_TYPE_HARDWARE was wrong in the first place and some
    HALs might not like it.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [leds] Add an alternate way to pass backlight info to the HAL.
    Some buggy HALs expect use a different way to set the brightness,
    and they do it by passing the actual value directly.
    Enable this by setting the "backlight-max-alternate" gsetting
    to a value > 0 (the actual max_value supported by your panel).
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [libdroid] Release 0.0.3.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [include] Move Light HAL specific stuff to libdroid-shared/leds-objects.h.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [libdroid] Allow implementing Android HALs.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [hals] Add a generic Light HAL.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [leds] hidl: try the libdroid slot first.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [leds] Switch hidl and aidl backends order.
    The libdroid generic HAL is HIDL, and we should prefer that
    if running.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [libdroid] Release 0.1.0.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [hals] common: utils: add droid_utils_file_exists.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [hals] lights: only check for file existence when looking at available lights.
    There might be some race conditions with Android init scripts (or port-specific
    stuff) where the HAL might start before the backlight panel node permissions
    have been adjusted.
    Assume we can write to the node if it exists, if we can't, we will catch
    the error anyway while actually trying to write there - so all good.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [hals] lights: set Restart=on-abnormal.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [libdroid] Release 0.1.1.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [hals] lights: add /sys/class/backlight/panel0-backlight to the list of known paths.
    Previously known as "fallback".
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [hals] lights: notifications: also check the result of the actual brightness change.
    We were only checking the breath/blink result previously.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [libdroid] Release 0.1.2.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [libdroid] Release 0.1.3.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [libdroid] Add DroidVibra and relative backends.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
  * [tools] Add libdroid-vibra-tool.
    Signed-off-by: Eugenio Paolantonio (g7) <me@medesimo.eu>
